<title>UK: Ladbroke takes charge after rent settlement.</title>
<headline>Ladbroke takes charge after rent settlement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hotel company Ladboke Group Plc said on Friday it had reached an out-of-court settlement in its rent review dispute with the landlord of the Paris Hilton.</p>
<p>The terms of the settlement will give rise to an exceptional charge of 16 million stg in the year to December 31 1996.</p>
<p>Ladbroke also said it had sold its Washington Vista Hotel for $47 million in cash to Interstate Hotels Company.</p>
</text>
